e Origin's Blue Moon lunar lander architecture","Blue Origin's first cargo Blue Moon lander, contracted under NASA's Commercial Lunar Payload Services (CLPS) program. A single-stage descent vehicle powered by the BE-7 cryogenic engine, designed to deliver up to ~3 tonnes of payload to the lunar surface. Launches on Blue Origin's New Glenn from Cape Canaveral, is left in low Earth orbit, then performs trans-lunar injection, lunar orbit insertion and powered descent on its own BE-7. The Mark 1 cargo flight precedes the human-rated Mark 2, which NASA contracted for crewed Artemis landings — now one of the two candidate landers for Artemis IV and later missions.",[497,501,504,507,510],{"met":55,"label":498,"note":499,"type":500},"NEW GLENN LAUNCH","Lifts off from Cape Canaveral LC-36; first stage returns for downrange recovery.","nominal",{"met":60,"label":502,"note":503,"type":500},"TLI","The lander's own BE-7 performs the trans-lunar injection burn; New Glenn left it in low Earth orbit.",{"met":65,"label":505,"note":506,"type":500},"TCM-1","First mid-course correction.",{"met":12,"label":508,"note":509,"type":500},"LOI","Lunar orbit insertion via BE-7 main engine.",{"met":74,"label":511,"note":512,"type":513},"POWERED DESCENT","BE-7 throttled descent to lunar surface — first Blue Origin lunar touchdown.","info","/orrery/images/missions/blue-moon-mk1/01.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
